        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Where There Is MSSQL, There Is A Way]]></title>
        <id>https://labs.reversec.com/posts/2026/05/where-there-is-mssql-there-is-a-way</id>
        <link href="https://labs.reversec.com/posts/2026/05/where-there-is-mssql-there-is-a-way"/>
        <updated>2026-05-04T00:00:00.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<div class="card-content"> <ul class="mt-6 mb-4 flex flex-wrap items-center text-text"> <li class="mr-5"> <a class="flex items-center hover:text-primary font-medium"> <img src="/_astro/alumnus.BuzBlUxW_ZE54yT.webp" alt="Max Keasley" class="mr-2 h-6 w-6 rounded-full" width="50" height="50" loading="lazy" decoding="async"> <span>Max Keasley</span> </a><a class="flex items-center hover:text-primary font-medium"> <img src="/_astro/owen-reeve.D3PhuptP_Z6UAIN.webp" alt="Owen Reeve" class="mr-2 h-6 w-6 rounded-full" width="50" height="50" loading="lazy" decoding="async"> <span>Owen Reeve</span> </a><a class="flex items-center hover:text-primary font-medium"> <img src="/_astro/sharan-patil.aUzMefiF_1hkGHj.webp" alt="Sharan Patil" class="mr-2 h-6 w-6 rounded-full" width="50" height="50" loading="lazy" decoding="async"> <span>Sharan Patil</span> </a> </li> <li class="mr-5 flex items-center flex-wrap font-medium"> <svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="mr-1 h-6 w-6 text-gray-500" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M19 4h-3V2h-2v2h-4V2H8v2H5c-1.103 0-2 .897-2 2v14c0 1.103.897 2 2 2h14c1.103 0 2-.897 2-2V6c0-1.103-.897-2-2-2zM5 20V7h14V6l.002 14H5z"></path><path d="m15.628 12.183-1.8-1.799 1.37-1.371 1.8 1.799zm-7.623 4.018V18h1.799l4.976-4.97-1.799-1.799z"></path></svg> <span>4 May 2026</span> </li> </ul> <h3 class="mb-4"> <a href="/posts/2026/05/where-there-is-mssql-there-is-a-way" class="block hover:text-primary transition duration-300"> Where There Is MSSQL, There Is A Way </a> </h3> <p class="summary">Authentication coercion via xp_dirtree and other stored procedures are well known tricks and are often blocked. What if we find other methods to capture Net-NTLMv2 hashes? As the latest organisation joining in the MSSQL EPA and NTLM relay research, we are here to highlight our journey of exploiting MSSQL NTLM Relay.</p> </div>]]></content>
    </entry>
